WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.200
SmartVest Investing Academy.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.375
Lesson 1: What is Investment?

3
00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:12.662
Have you ever wondered what actually happens when you invest money instead of just saving it?

4
00:00:12.662 --> 00:00:20.137
Saving means keeping your money safe—for example, in a bank savings account or a cash locker.

5
00:00:20.137 --> 00:00:27.625
While saving protects your nominal capital, inflation gradually reduces what that money can buy over time.

6
00:00:27.625 --> 00:00:42.587
Investing, on the other hand, means putting your money into assets—such as company stocks, bonds, mutual funds, or real estate—with the expectation that they may generate income or grow in value over time.

7
00:00:42.587 --> 00:00:46.725
For example, imagine you have ₹10,000.

8
00:00:46.725 --> 00:00:55.475
If you leave it in a zero-interest locker for 5 years, it will still be ₹10,000, but groceries and rent will cost more.

9
00:00:55.475 --> 00:01:05.825
If you invest that ₹10,000 in productive businesses or diversified funds, your capital has the potential to grow alongside the economy.

10
00:01:05.825 --> 00:01:11.575
Remember: investing involves risk, and asset values can fluctuate.

11
00:01:11.575 --> 00:01:19.825
The goal of investing is to balance risk and potential growth so your wealth maintains its purchasing power over the long term.

12
00:01:19.825 --> 00:01:22.875
SmartVest Investing Academy.

13
00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:24.700
Learn first.

14
00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:27.150
Invest with understanding.
